    "body": "The public repository landing page still describes 0.2.0 while v0.3.0 and its operator/source downloads are already published. Promote the released BASE1 source, Python serial terminal, migration tools, user manual and scoped hardware evidence to main.\n\nThe README now says “4KB of firmware. One board. Up to four boot environments.” The adjacent explanation states that compatible user-supplied images run one at a time on shared CPU, RAM and peripherals. Main is the current release/integration branch; Mona and future ABI changes use feature branches. The immutable v0.3.0 tag and published ZIPs stay unchanged.\n\nValidation: frozen-F/component/source/host integrity passed; prior package extraction and exact rc1 runtime equivalence receipts are included. Reviewed 2512 hardware cases and the 2609 extracted-rc1 existing-SNBT upgrade retain their original scopes. No new build, simulation or board access. F remains exactly 4096 bytes, SHA-256 8f4d35ac66730daa773515980983fcf442be3b1bdf1e523d3752ec3615657cc1. Final-package live trials and the WDC/programmer-F package routes remain NOT RUN.\n\nThe current main 0.2.0 tree was verified identical to the 0.2.0 baseline already in this branch. A history-only merge reconciles that squash without changing the reviewed release tree.",
